summary:
  A station's start hands the cover that is on screen to the cast device
  without asking whether it belongs to the station that is starting.

history:
  The start used to send the station's list icon and nothing else (32 by
  32 pixels on one station, measured 2026-11-11, stretched over a
  television). It now asks CastLogic.picture, so a cover that is known
  wins over the icon. At a switch to another station the cover on screen
  is still the previous station's track, and a device keeps the picture it
  was sent for as long as the station plays, so the cover goes in only
  when the station starting is the one already on. This mutant sends it
  along with any station.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
                            CastLogic.picture("", station.name === root.currentStation ? root.trackArtUrl : "", station.favicon));

replace:
                            CastLogic.picture("", root.trackArtUrl, station.favicon));

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_the_picture_a_device_is_sent_is_chosen_in_one_place.
  Line-neutral.
